From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: keep the Ethernet XSI MAC out of reset on reopen

Every ndo_open runs phylink_start(), whose major configuration calls
pcs_pre_config(). On the Ethernet PCS this pulses the SCU XSI MAC/PHY
resets and the XFI MAC logic reset each time the port is brought up,
even when the interface mode does not change. When offloaded traffic
keeps arriving while the port is down, the GDM feeding the MAC holds a
frame from its output queue across these resets, and once the link is
back its TX channel locks up for good: MBI_TX_BUSY stays set, the MAC
transmits nothing and only a reboot recovers the port.

The resets are only needed to select the XSI mode, so skip them and the
counter clear when the Ethernet PCS is reconfigured for the interface
it already runs. The first configuration and any interface change still
reset the XSI MAC and PHY as before, and the PON PCS is left unchanged.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -914,11 +914,15 @@ static void airoha_pcs_pre_config(struct
 	struct airoha_pcs_port *port = to_airoha_pcs_port(pcs);
 	struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv = port->priv;
 	struct airoha_pcs_maps *maps;
+	bool full_reset;
 
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
+	full_reset = priv->data->port_type != AIROHA_PCS_ETH ||
+		     priv->interface != interface;
 
 	/* Select HSGMII or USXGMII in SCU regs */
-	airoha_pcs_setup_scu(priv, port->index, interface);
+	if (full_reset)
+		airoha_pcs_setup_scu(priv, port->index, interface);
 
 	/* MPI MBI disable */
 	regmap_set_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
@@ -927,6 +931,9 @@ static void airoha_pcs_pre_config(struct
 			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TXMPI_STOP |
 			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TXMBI_STOP);
 
+	if (!full_reset)
+		return;
+
 	/* Write 1 to trigger reset and clear */
 	regmap_clear_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_LOGIC_RST,
 			  AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_LOGIC_RST);
